  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let the roots of \\(ax^2+bx+c=0\\) be \\(r\\) and \\(s.\\) The equation with roots \\(ar+b\\) and \\(as+b\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(x^2-bx-ac=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(x^2-bx+ac=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(x^2+3bx+ca+2b^2=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(x^2+3bx-ca+2b^2=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\begin{gathered}x^2+bx(2-a)\\\\{}+a^2c+b^2(a+1)=0\\end{gathered}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1961-p29.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The transformed roots have sum \\[ a(r+s)+2b=-b+2b=b \\] and product \\[ \\begin{gathered} (ar+b)(as+b)\\\\ =a^2rs+ab(r+s)+b^2\\\\ =ac. \\end{gathered} \\] Therefore their monic equation is \\(x^2-bx+ac=0.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(r+s=-\\frac{b}{a}\\) and \\(rs=\\frac{c}{a}\\)",
        "Compute the sum and product of \\(ar+b\\) and \\(as+b\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
